00:01:53.750 --> 00:01:56.590
Log Horizon Guild 
Hall - Akiba

00:01:54.310 --> 00:01:57.060
Shiro went to the Guild Building again, huh?

00:01:57.060 --> 00:02:01.690
He's purrty busy with preparing for the
New Round Table Conference every day.

00:02:01.690 --> 00:02:04.440
I haven't seen his face for a long time.

00:02:04.440 --> 00:02:07.560
Don't talk like he's a father who lives
apart from his family due to his job.

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:09.060
Tada!

00:02:09.060 --> 00:02:11.310
That's... the Kanami puppet!

00:02:11.310 --> 00:02:13.020
Ding, ding, ding, ding!

00:02:13.020 --> 00:02:17.020
Hey, hey, Naotsugu. I wanna ask you something.

00:02:17.020 --> 00:02:17.900
What is it?

00:02:17.900 --> 00:02:23.690
I'll cut to the chase.
Was Kanami Shiroe's girlfriend?

00:02:23.690 --> 00:02:25.230
Hmm...

00:02:25.230 --> 00:02:26.600
Oh?

00:02:27.560 --> 00:02:30.230
I guess... it's about time, huh?

00:02:30.230 --> 00:02:32.190
Yeah.

00:02:32.190 --> 00:02:37.520
Well, I don't think she was.
Actually, it clearly wasn't the case.

00:02:37.520 --> 00:02:41.440
If they were dating, his stomach
wouldn't have survived from all that stress.

00:02:41.440 --> 00:02:43.980
His life could've even been in danger.

00:02:43.980 --> 00:02:45.480
Is that right?

00:02:45.480 --> 00:02:49.190
They weren't in that kind of relationship.

00:02:49.190 --> 00:02:52.730
She's like his older sister.

00:02:52.730 --> 00:02:59.020
But, well... Shiro might've
been in love with Kanami.

00:02:59.020 --> 00:03:02.150
You are quite calm, Akatsuki.

00:03:02.150 --> 00:03:04.270
The past is the past, after all.

00:03:05.310 --> 00:03:10.690
I actually feel better. It's much
better than not knowing about it.

00:03:10.690 --> 00:03:11.940
Oomph!

00:03:11.940 --> 00:03:14.900
I see... Then I'll give this to you, Naotsugu.

00:03:14.900 --> 00:03:16.190
No thanks.

00:03:16.190 --> 00:03:18.650
Then who shall I give this to?

00:03:19.270 --> 00:03:22.890
Guild Building - Akiba

00:03:22.600 --> 00:03:25.980
Shiroe! I brought the report!

00:03:25.980 --> 00:03:28.100
Shiro... e...?

00:03:28.100 --> 00:03:30.850
Yeah...

00:03:28.350 --> 00:03:30.980
Astral Projection

00:03:31.020 --> 00:03:36.980
The Oldest Ancients

00:03:33.520 --> 00:03:36.230
"The Oldest Ancients."

00:03:36.980 --> 00:03:40.240
m 872 0 l 1278 0 1278 94 872 94

00:03:36.980 --> 00:03:40.240
City Planning (Villain) Division
Please kn̷o̷ick   Heh-heh-heh

00:03:36.980 --> 00:03:40.240
m 523 454 l 498 454 503 478 504 495 499 494 496 459 496 453 450 460 448 454 492 450 485 410 490 410 497 447 523 450

00:03:38.270 --> 00:03:41.980
Working in the City Planning Division
seems like a lot of work.

00:03:41.980 --> 00:03:44.650
Actually, it's mostly odd jobs.

00:03:44.650 --> 00:03:50.310
People just bring their problems to us
on the pretext of building a better Akiba.

00:03:50.310 --> 00:03:53.730
If I could help him more...

00:03:53.730 --> 00:03:55.730
What's your current concern?

00:03:55.730 --> 00:03:57.770
Hmm... Let's see...

00:03:57.770 --> 00:04:00.150
For midterm issues, I think there are three.

00:04:00.150 --> 00:04:01.560
Three?

00:04:01.560 --> 00:04:04.400
First, the relationship with Westelande.

00:04:04.400 --> 00:04:08.230
Things have gotten complicated,
on top of the matters with the Saiguu Family.

00:04:08.230 --> 00:04:09.770
I see.

00:04:09.770 --> 00:04:11.980
Next, the communication with the moon.

00:04:11.980 --> 00:04:15.850
There may be enemies there, too,
but being able to get info would be a big win.

00:04:15.850 --> 00:04:20.810
But it costs a lot of money
to build this huge antenna, right?

00:04:20.810 --> 00:04:23.020
Money <i>and</i> technology.

00:04:23.020 --> 00:04:27.810
But Akiba now has about 100,000 pioneers.
It's no longer impossible.

00:04:27.810 --> 00:04:31.940
Oh, right. It grew larger in scale, so...

00:04:31.940 --> 00:04:33.900
Third, Geniuses.

00:04:33.900 --> 00:04:35.900
Besides the ones we've faced,

00:04:35.900 --> 00:04:39.560
ones with various other characteristics
have also been observed.

00:04:39.560 --> 00:04:41.810
So we still need to be cautious.

00:04:41.810 --> 00:04:43.520
Yeah.

00:04:43.520 --> 00:04:47.650
You guys did a very good job
in the Shibuya Raid, too.

00:04:47.650 --> 00:04:50.060
To be honest, it is of great help.

00:04:50.060 --> 00:04:56.020
Well, everything is thanks to you
for rescuing us from Hamelin.

00:04:56.020 --> 00:05:00.440
Me, Toya, and the others are very grateful.

00:05:00.440 --> 00:05:04.150
Really... she's become strong.

00:05:04.600 --> 00:05:06.440
Head Splitter!

00:05:06.440 --> 00:05:09.940
Excellent, Mr. Toya.

00:05:09.940 --> 00:05:12.100
I think this is enough for today.

00:05:12.100 --> 00:05:14.520
We've got a bountiful harvest!

00:05:14.710 --> 00:05:21.250
Harmocross Islet

00:05:14.710 --> 00:05:21.250
